#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c084ff9-c7b2-5468-96fa-62c7fc1ff782" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,-78,13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303462} {:answer/id #uuid "813c003b-ef4c-5693-9b5f-7a04ada2b1bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,78,-13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303463} {:answer/id #uuid "2020b3ba-da42-5e2b-afa8-ba14436030e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,78,-13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303464} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7908e0-f75a-5388-a30b-8a5006b8643f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,0,-13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303465} {:answer/id #uuid "5703efa3-065b-5370-8e96-92e7b4faf301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,78,13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2020b3ba-da42-5e2b-afa8-ba14436030e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,78,-13⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303464} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f95e987-f817-53b2-9aea-39e647ca85ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0862516a-638f-50dc-ae6f-b2e60f0dfa5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-1407" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨0,1,6⟩$ and $b=⟨13,0,0⟩.$ Find $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 13 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 13 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 13 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 0-6\\cdot 0)i-(0\\cdot 0-6\\cdot 13)j+(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 13)k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-78)j+(0-13)k \\\\  & =78j-13k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5155a28-22dd-54d9-904d-52eb3db422cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5155a28-22dd-54d9-904d-52eb3db422cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303496} :answer-field/id #uuid "50096657-96ad-5bc8-923d-da3a399564ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c56013b-cca9-556f-bfe4-7260efbe46bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c56013b-cca9-556f-bfe4-7260efbe46bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303498} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e24a0b4-61de-584c-94ac-928507f054ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a06a34cd-d85e-589e-9964-4d0cd1f43e22" :question/math-academy-id "q-282262" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,3,0⟩,$ $b=⟨-x,0,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{49}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 0 \\\\ -x & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 0 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ -x & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-0)i-(x+0)j+(0+3x)k \\\\  & =⟨3,-x,3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-x)^{2}+(3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9} & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\ 10{x}^{2}+9 & =49 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-2,$ $x=2.$"}]}
